1
00:00:03,207 --> 00:00:05,985
Every team has three versions of revenue, and

2
00:00:05,985 --> 00:00:08,577
nobody knows which one the dashboard uses.

3
00:00:09,027 --> 00:00:12,608
Metric Dictionary lays every metric out as a periodic

4
00:00:12,608 --> 00:00:16,527
table: one element per metric, grouped by business domain.

5
00:00:16,977 --> 00:00:21,190
The finish is the status: solid is approved, outlined is

6
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:25,327
in review, hatched is a draft, and faded is deprecated.

7
00:00:26,448 --> 00:00:31,547
Lenses re-colour the same table: by status, by owner, and

8
00:00:31,547 --> 00:00:36,378
by freshness, the days since each metric last changed.

9
00:00:38,457 --> 00:00:42,284
The Today panel ranks what needs a steward. Gross

10
00:00:42,284 --> 00:00:46,267
Margin version 1.1 would change an approved metric.

11
00:00:46,717 --> 00:00:49,415
One click focuses that element and opens

12
00:00:49,415 --> 00:00:52,247
a preview with its definition and formula.

13
00:00:53,055 --> 00:00:56,240
The element card holds the definition, the formula in

14
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:59,305
business words, and the measure that implements it.

15
00:00:59,755 --> 00:01:02,718
Its isotopes are the versions, and each one

16
00:01:02,718 --> 00:01:06,025
opens as tracked changes against the one before.

17
00:01:07,997 --> 00:01:11,926
View as owner dims everything that is not yours, so Sam

18
00:01:11,926 --> 00:01:15,497
sees his own elements and what they need from him.

19
00:01:18,351 --> 00:01:21,544
In the Lab, Sam proposes a new metric. The element

20
00:01:21,544 --> 00:01:24,801
preview and the duplicate check update as he types.

21
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:29,266
Churned revenue overlaps with Customer Churn Rate and Revenue,

22
00:01:29,266 --> 00:01:32,051
so he can read those before adding another.

23
00:01:32,501 --> 00:01:34,650
He saves it as a draft, and it

24
00:01:34,650 --> 00:01:37,301
joins the table as a hatched element.

25
00:01:38,105 --> 00:01:40,990
Stewards approve in Peer review, where a re-review

26
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:44,105
shows exactly what changed since the approved version.

27
00:01:44,908 --> 00:01:50,848
Approved elements export as a printable poster, a Markdown table or a CSV.

28
00:01:51,652 --> 00:01:55,234
One definition per metric, one owner and one approval

29
00:01:55,234 --> 00:01:58,072
trail, running as a Fabric App in preview.
